      "question": {
        "id": "E06",
        "question": "The ETH guide is dated 2023 but now says both 0.1 and 0.01 ETH. What minimum applies to a new stake on 12 September 2026, since when, and what does 32 ETH refer to?",
        "reference": "New stakes use 0.01 ETH from June 2026. The older 0.1 text remains. 32 ETH is the pooled validator activation threshold, not the retail minimum.",
        "referenceUrls": [
          "https://everstake.com/resources/blog/how-to-stake-01-ether-or-more-on-the-everstake-website",
          "https://everstake.com/staking/protocols/ethereum"
        ],
        "difficulty": "hard",
        "category": "temporal_conflict",
        "whyHard": "Do not date the 0.01 change to 2023 or call 32 ETH the retail minimum.",
        "negative": false,
        "rubric": [
          "Do not date the 0.01 change to 2023 or call 32 ETH the retail minimum."
        ]
      },
      "answer": {
        "runId": "1b68d579-3952-4fdf-9888-fb3107b1773d",
        "status": "answered",
        "question": "The ETH guide is dated 2023 but now says both 0.1 and 0.01 ETH. What minimum applies to a new stake on 12 September 2026, since when, and what does 32 ETH refer to?",
        "text": "Everstake's minimum staking requirement for new stakes is 0.01 ETH. [01fb27ed221b9d386699278e013c4598] [17f5853119a054335b8027ebadeb3842]\n\nThe 0.01 ETH minimum applies to new stakes as of June 2026, announced on June 18, 2026, lowering the previous 0.1 ETH threshold introduced on September 14, 2023. [01fb27ed221b9d386699278e013c4598] [17f5853119a054335b8027ebadeb3842]\n\nThe 32 ETH figure refers to the Ethereum protocol's native network requirement to launch and activate a validator. [17f5853119a054335b8027ebadeb3842] [1515f9ec9aade0f4da0c505c27cfcf70]",
        "asOf": "2026-09-09",
