          },
          {
            "id": "17f5853119a054335b8027ebadeb3842",
            "documentId": "45cadbbdbaf9713824124b9b16a5cb8a",
            "url": "https://everstake.com/resources/blog/everstake-lowers-the-ethereum-staking-minimum-to-0-01-eth",
            "title": "Everstake Lowers the Ethereum Staking Minimum to 0.01 ETH | Everstake",
            "text": "Company News\nethereum\n\n# Everstake Lowers the Ethereum Staking Minimum to 0.01 ETH\n\n## Everstake has lowered the minimum for our non-custodial Ethereum staking solution from 0.1 ETH to 0.01 ETH.\nJUN 18, 2026\nLast updated SEP 09, 2026 · V1\nShare with your network\nTable of Contents\nTL;DR\nWhy Use Everstake’s 0.01+ ETH Staking Solution\nHow to stake Ethereum starting from 0.01 ETH\nHow the 0.01+ ETH Staking Solution Works\nFAQ\nShow\n\n## TL;DR\n- You can now stake from 0.01 ETH with Everstake, a non-custodial staking provider founded in 2018.\n- Everstake simplifies the entry to staking, while validator activation remains subject to the Ethereum protocol’s 32 ETH requirement.\n- Assets stay in your wallet, withdrawals can be initiated anytime, and the solution is audited by ChainSecurity, Ackee, Trail of Bits.\n- Users can start staking through theEverstake ETH staking (https://stake.everstake.one/dashboard/stake/ethereum)dashboard in a few steps.\nThe previous threshold, introduced on September 14, 2023, already reduced the native 32 ETH validator requirement 320 times. The new minimum lowers it 3,200 times.\nA lower entry threshold means more holders can participate in securing the Ethereum network. Broader participation supports decentralization across the validator set.",
            "authority": 1,
            "publisher": "Everstake",
            "publishedAt": "2026-06-18T17:00:27.000Z",
            "updatedAt": "2026-09-09T00:00:00.000Z",
            "fetchedAt": "2026-09-13T14:01:56.685Z",
            "duplicateGroup": "45cadbbdbaf9713824124b9b16a5cb8a",
            "score": 0.031818181818181815,
            "reason": "Lexical and semantic rank fusion; diversified by content group. Authority and temporal validity checked separately.",
            "metadata": {
              "sourceId": "everstake-com"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "1515f9ec9aade0f4da0c505c27cfcf70",
            "documentId": "b905fd39b215735727a8f0f716d06578",
            "url": "https://everstake.com/resources/blog/everstake-makes-ethereum-staking-accessible-and-high-yielding-to-everyone",
            "title": "Everstake Makes Ethereum Staking Accessible and High-yielding to Everyone | Everstake",
            "text": "ethereum\n\n# Everstake Makes Ethereum Staking Accessible and High-yielding to Everyone\n\n## Everstake is thrilled to announce the release of its 0.1+ ETH staking solution, the world’s first non-custodial service enabling anyone to stake as little as 0.1 ETH.\nSEP 14, 2023\nLast updated JUN 19, 2026 · V1\nShare with your network\nTable of Contents\nWhy Use Everstake’s 0.1+ ETH Staking Solution\nHow to stake Ethereum starting from 0.1 ETH\nHow the 0.1+ ETH Staking Solution Works\nShow\nWe’re thrilled to announce the release of our 0.1+ ETH staking (https://stake.everstake.one/ethereum/), a non-custodial service enabling anyone to stake as little as 0.1 ETH. We’re pretty thrilled to be the first ones to do it!\nNOTE: As of June 2026, the minimum to stake ETH with Everstake is 0.01 ETH, down from 0.1 ETH. The new minimum applies to new stakes only. Figures and screenshots elsewhere in this article may still reflect the old 0.1 ETH minimum. See current minimums on the ETH staking page (https://everstake.one/staking/protocols/ethereum).\nAfter Ethereum became a Proof-of-Stake blockchain, everyone was waiting for ETH’s staking to become a reality. Still, the network’s rules demand that the minimum stake to launch a validator is 32 ETH, which may be too high of a threshold for many potential stakers.\nWith Everstake’s solution, this entry threshold is lowered 320 times.",
            "authority": 1,
